  "answer": "Based on the deep research across all five queries, I have the complete picture. Let me synthesize the findings:\n\n## Answer: **Norway**\n\n### Summary of Evidence\n\n**US Baseline Values (from OWID):**\n- LGBT+ rights index (2019): **7.084** [1]\n- Women's business and the law index (2023): **91.25** [2]\n- Annual working hours per worker (2017): **1,795.58 hours** [3]\n\n**Intersection of Countries Beating US on All Three Metrics (11 countries):**\nBelgium, Denmark, France, Germany, Iceland, Luxembourg, Netherlands, Norway, Portugal, Spain, Sweden [4][5][6]\n\n**2022 Happiness Share with Positive Relative Change (from OWID \"Share of people who say they are happy\"):**\n\n| Country | 2022 Happiness % | Relative Change |\n|---------|------------------|-----------------|\n| **Norway** | **94.06%** | **+2.02%** |\n| France | 90.88% | +2.19% |\n| Germany | 86.40% | +9.17% |\n| Portugal | 87.79% | +20.65% |\n| Spain | 88.79% | +14.20% |\n\n[7][8]\n\n**Norway** has the highest happiness share (94.06%) among all qualifying countries that also show a positive relative change from the earliest survey year to 2022.\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/lgbt-rights-index.csv — US 2019 value: 7.0840597  \n[2] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/women-business-and-the-law-index.csv — US 2023 value: 91.25  \n[3] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-working-hours-per-worker.csv — US 2017 value: 1795.58 hours  \n[4] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/lgbt-rights-index — LGBT+ rights index dataset (Velasco 2020)  \n[5] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/women-business-and-the-law-index — Women, Business and the Law index (World Bank)  \n[6] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-working-hours-per-worker — Annual working hours (Penn World Table)  \n[7] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-people-who-say-they-are-happy — Happiness share dataset (Integrated Values Surveys)  \n[8] https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-people-who-say-